WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:12.347
Suddenly, Duman the storyteller threw his handkerchief in the air.

2
00:00:12.348 --> 00:00:16.333
He wanted to change the mood and amuse the guards.

3
00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:22.171
The men looked up and forgot about the children for a moment.

4
00:00:22.172 --> 00:00:25.213
"Run!" shouted Vinnie.

5
00:00:25.214 --> 00:00:29.219
Mandy grabbed her mother's earrings from the guard.

6
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.617
Berk didn't have time to grab his silver.

7
00:00:32.618 --> 00:00:36.236
The children ran out of the coffee shop.

8
00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:38.879
They thought the guards would chase them.

9
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.888
The children ran up one street and down another.

10
00:00:42.889 --> 00:00:48.646
Finally they stopped, gasping for breath.

11
00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:53.529
"Do you hear that music?" said Mandy.

12
00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.801
"We can't stop to listen!" Berk said sharply.

13
00:00:57.802 --> 00:01:01.004
"I need to go back to the bazaar right away."

14
00:01:01.005 --> 00:01:04.950
"Wait just a minute," Mandy insisted.

15
00:01:04.951 --> 00:01:11.415
She and Vinnie walked toward the music, and Berk slowly followed.

16
00:01:11.416 --> 00:01:15.303
"What's going on?" Mandy asked.

17
00:01:15.304 --> 00:01:19.485
They saw musicians and dancers in an open field.

18
00:01:19.486 --> 00:01:21.477
Food was being served.

19
00:01:21.478 --> 00:01:23.620
Everything smelled good.

20
00:01:23.621 --> 00:01:27.879
"A wrestling match is about to begin," said Berk.

21
00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:31.473
"Can we stay and watch?" asked Vinnie.

22
00:01:31.474 --> 00:01:34.356
Berk looked around nervously.

23
00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:37.353
He thought the guards might be nearby.

24
00:01:37.354 --> 00:01:38.890
"No, we shouldn't.

25
00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:43.008
These matches can last for days," Berk replied.

26
00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:47.212
A loud horn signaled the beginning of the match.

27
00:01:47.213 --> 00:01:51.014
Two big men walked to the middle of the crowd.

28
00:01:51.015 --> 00:01:55.607
People cheered and shouted as they watched the wrestlers.

29
00:01:55.608 --> 00:01:59.867
"Please, we must leave," said Berk.

30
00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:04.080
He motioned for Vinnie and Mandy to follow him.

31
00:02:04.081 --> 00:02:07.139
They returned to the Grand Bazaar.

32
00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:11.213
Berk explained to his father what had happened.

33
00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.676
"The sultan's guards are fair men.

34
00:02:13.677 --> 00:02:17.011
They will give back the silver," said Ali.

35
00:02:17.012 --> 00:02:19.348
"Let me see the earrings."

36
00:02:19.349 --> 00:02:21.882
He took them from Mandy.

37
00:02:21.883 --> 00:02:25.000
"Where did you get these?" he asked.

38
00:02:25.001 --> 00:02:28.308
"They're my mother's," Mandy replied.

39
00:02:28.309 --> 00:02:30.606
"I didn't steal them."

40
00:02:30.607 --> 00:02:33.155
Ali looked at Mandy and said,

41
00:02:33.156 --> 00:02:35.554
"I'm worried about you."

42
00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.216
"Why?" asked Vinnie.

43
00:02:38.217 --> 00:02:43.470
"You are strangers and these earrings look expensive," said Ali.

44
00:02:43.471 --> 00:02:46.816
"The Janissary won't stop looking for you."

45
00:02:46.817 --> 00:02:49.285
Vinnie gulped loudly.

46
00:02:49.286 --> 00:02:54.561
"But we didn't do anything wrong!" he cried.

47
00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:58.537
"You took back the earrings and ran away," said Ali.

48
00:02:58.538 --> 00:03:01.014
"They think you are hiding something."

49
00:03:01.015 --> 00:03:04.808
Just then they heard loud voices.

50
00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:07.544
"They're here!" cried Berk.

51
00:03:07.545 --> 00:03:10.171
He hid behind his father.

52
00:03:10.172 --> 00:03:14.009
The guards from the coffee shop came into the bazaar.

53
00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:20.550
They stopped at every shop to look for the children behind curtains and under tables.

54
00:03:20.551 --> 00:03:23.937
"We have to go, Mandy," Vinnie said.

55
00:03:23.938 --> 00:03:26.085
"We can't stay here!"

56
00:03:26.086 --> 00:03:30.942
"Thank you for your help," Mandy said to Berk and his family.

57
00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:34.597
"We're sorry for any trouble we caused."

58
00:03:34.598 --> 00:03:38.402
"May Allah give you peace," said Berk.

59
00:03:38.403 --> 00:03:41.881
"Pray to Allah and all will be well."

60
00:03:41.882 --> 00:03:44.534
Vinnie and Mandy turned to leave.

61
00:03:44.535 --> 00:03:47.547
But Vinnie tripped over a carpet.

62
00:03:47.548 --> 00:03:51.881
He bumped into a table with colorful tiles on display.

63
00:03:51.882 --> 00:03:55.016
Everything fell with a loud crash.

64
00:03:55.017 --> 00:04:04.256
"There they are!" shouted the guards. "Stop, thieves!"
